From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Connolly <david@connol.ly>
Date: Thu, 06 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] mb/asrock/z77_extreme4: XE stability tuning for
 overclocked operation

Configure stability-related settings for overclocked Sandy/Ivy
Bridge operation on the Z77 Extreme4:

1. PP0 (vCore) current limit: 130A

   The default Icc limit of 112A in the coreboot code matches the
   Intel stock TDP spec.  The Z77 Extreme4's ISL6367-based VRM is
   capable of ~130A sustained.  At elevated turbo ratios (44x 1C/2C,
   42x 3C/4C) with PL1=165W, transient current spikes during burst
   load onset can exceed 112A, triggering the CPU's internal current
   throttle and causing sudden clock drops.

2. Package C-state limit: 0 (PC0/PC1 only)

   Prevents the package from entering deep C-states (PC6/PC7)
   which require large voltage rail transitions on wake.  Keeps the
   VRM in a steady operating region.

3. Energy-Performance Bias: 0 (performance)

   Makes the hardware P-state controller react as fast as possible
   to load changes, minimising time at intermediate voltage/frequency
   points during ramp-up to turbo ratios.

4. ACPI C-state limit: 1 (C1 only)

   Advertises only C1 in the ACPI _CST table, preventing Windows
   and other ACPI-aware OSes from requesting deep core C-states
   (CC3/CC6/CC7).  Linux intel_idle bypasses _CST, so Linux users
   should also set intel_idle.max_cstate=1 on the kernel cmdline.

These settings prioritise stability and latency over idle power
savings, matching the intended use case of an overclocked desktop
with high-end air cooling.

Depends on:
  cpu/intel/model_206ax: add configurable package C-state limit
  cpu/intel/model_206ax: add configurable energy-performance bias
  cpu/intel/model_206ax: add configurable ACPI C-state limit
  mb/asrock/z77_extreme4: configure CPU power limits via devicetree

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000014
Signed-off-by: David Connolly <david@connol.ly>
---
 src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/Kconfig      | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/devicetree.cb |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/Kconfig b/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/Kconfig
index 7777777777..8888888888 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/Kconfig
+++ b/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/Kconfig
@@ -3,4 +3,16 @@ if BOARD_ASROCK_Z77_EXTREME4
 # existing board Kconfig content ...
 
+config PKG_CSTATE_LIMIT
+	int
+	default 0
+
+config ENERGY_PERF_BIAS
+	int
+	default 0
+
+config ACPI_CSTATE_LIMIT
+	int
+	default 1
+
 endif # BOARD_ASROCK_Z77_EXTREME4
diff --git a/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/devicetree.cb
index 6666666666..7777777777 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/asrock/z77_extreme4/devicetree.cb
@@ -12,6 +12,9 @@
 		# PL2 (burst): 200W — allows full turbo headroom during burst loads
 		register "pl2_mw" = "200000"
 		register "pl2_clamp" = "1"
+
+		# PP0 vCore current limit: 130A (ISL6367 4-phase VRM capability)
+		register "pp0_current_limit" = "130"
 
 		device cpu_cluster 0 on end
 	end
